flowchart TB
  accTitle: How the numbers get onto the accuracy page
  accDescr: A maintainer starts the workflow Evaluate by hand with a repository and a number of issues. The job replay, on the egress-firewall runner with a read-only token and the engine's secret, runs evaluate against a checkout of that repository and keeps its report as an artifact. The job publish runs no AI: accuracy-page takes only numbers and names from the report, and refuses a report that has anything else. The release app adds them to one pull request, which a person merges, and the website shows the table.
  start(["a maintainer runs<br>the workflow Evaluate:<br>repository, 30 issues"]) --> replay["`**job replay**, with the AI:<br>egress-firewall runner,<br>read-only token,<br>the engine's secret`"]
  replay --> report[("the report,<br>an artifact")]
  report --> check{"`**job publish**, no AI:<br>accuracy-page finds only<br>numbers and names?`"}
  check -- "no" --> refused["refused:<br>the page stays"]
  check -- "yes" --> pull["`**one pull request**<br>of the release app,<br>which each run adds to`"]
  pull --> merge["a person merges"]
  merge --> website[("the table of the<br>repository on the website")]
  classDef trigger fill:#d4a72c33,stroke:#bf8700,stroke-width:2px
  classDef question fill:#d4a72c33,stroke:#bf8700,stroke-width:2px
  classDef job fill:#8c959f1f,stroke:#8c959f,stroke-width:2px
  classDef safe fill:#1a7f3726,stroke:#1a7f37,stroke-width:2px
  class start trigger
  class check question
  class replay,pull,merge,refused job
  class report,website safe
